{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1287660-mage-armor-piercing","id":1287660,"title":"Mage Armor Piercing","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-13T13:56:40-08:00","id":1287660,"title":"Mage Armor Piercing","content":"Hey everyone,<br /> <br /> So I have wondered about this particular attainment often and I want to think there should be an ability to pierce mage armor. Maybe it is just a mindset left over from 1E where they were spells, but I feel like Mage Armor being a perfect set of armor with no way to negate seems a bit odd to me. Perhaps that is the new thing with attainments or a way to discourage fights, but it just seems there should be away. Anyone have any house rules on this?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T14:12:48-08:00","id":1287666,"title":"","content":"I mean, you could always circumvent any particular Mage Armor by using attacks that it doesn't apply to. Or you could just deal more damage. They're capped at 5/0 armor at mastery levels and second edition damage sums successes and damage modifier (except for attack spells that use Potency but they also circumvent most Mage Armor anyway) so basically everything has potential to deal damage in excess of even a Master's Mage Armor.<br /> <br /> Edit: I guess what I'm saying is that Mage Armor just isn't potent enough to require ways to negate it. Unlike spells and attacks they're capped, and they're not universally applicable either (except maybe Death, I don't recall how that worked).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 02-13-2019, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T14:47:36-08:00","id":1287681,"title":"","content":"Hey Tessie,<br /> <br /> Here are some quotes for each armor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Death Armor downgrades lethal damage from kinetic attacks (bullets, claws, rocks, etc.) to bashing. A mage using Death Armor does not roll to stay conscious once her Health track is filled with damage. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Forces Armor applies the mage\u2019s full Forces rating as general armor, applicable against all damaging physical attacks and the automatic damage from fire and electricity. It has no effect on mental or psychic attacks. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Life Armor adds half the character\u2019s Life rating (round up) as both general armor and a bonus to Defense. Use the higher of the character\u2019s Wits and Dexterity as Defense, rather than the lower. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Matter Armor applies the mage\u2019s full Matter rating as general armor, applicable against all damaging physical attacks. It is immune to Armor Piercing. Matter Armor has no effect on mental or psychic attacks. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Spirit Armor downgrades lethal damage from kinetic attacks (bullets, claws, rocks, etc.) and the attacks of ephemeral entities to bashing. </div> </div> </div>Half seem to have some type of damage degrading/ignoring capabilities. Acanthus and Mastigos being the only Mages left with just a pure defense method which could arguably be even better since a defense of 6 or higher is pretty much impossible to hit when using mundane folks.<br /> <br /> *shrugs* I mean, I guess if you have a military grade weapons you might be able to dent a mage. Forces 3 generates 3 armor which makes it pretty unlikely anything but a large military grade weapon will do anything. My main concern is because Seers like to use proxies and it seems without having some pretty heavy packing proxies, there really is no point in having them at all. In 1E when armor could be dispelled it made proxy encounters orchestrated by Seers deadly, but now it is just like, &quot;Meh. I can throw up Forces Armor and your goons are going to need to pull out the military grade stuff just to scratch me.&quot; Because, again, even if you have AP bullets doesn't matter against mage armor. Also, unless you have highly skilled proxies there are never going to get above that threshold unless they are carrying some pretty heavy damaging weapons.<br /> <br /> One could argue maybe they do some autofire or teamwork fire (not sure if that is a thing), but again that is a lot of focus for just one mage.<br /> <br /> Just feels odd to me that mundanes have literally no chance against damaging mages at all anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":". 02-13-2019, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T15:22:40-08:00","id":1287703,"title":"","content":"If it helps, I'm pretty certain that direct damage spells bypass Mage Armor (except for Prime), so there's that. I could also envision an alternate Prime Utility Attainment that lets a mage either ignore Mage Armor for an attack or negate it for the scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T15:24:45-08:00","id":1287705,"title":"","content":"You hit a Mage before they can get their armor up, then you never have to worry about piercing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T15:34:25-08:00","id":1287711,"title":"","content":"Flame thrower","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9015-zee-patrick","name":"zee PaTrick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T15:40:24-08:00","id":1287714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1287660-mage-armor-piercing?p=1287705#post1287705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You hit a Mage before they can get their armor up, then you never have to worry about piercing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possible, but extremely rare and it is a reflexive action to activate. I mean, you might be able to get a Stealth check to use it, but you better hope the one shot drops them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Flame thrower </div> </div> </div>Yeah, military grade weaponry as I mentioned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it helps, I'm pretty certain that direct damage spells bypass Mage Armor (except for Prime), so there's that. I could also envision an alternate Prime Utility Attainment that lets a mage either ignore Mage Armor for an attack or negate it for the scene. </div> </div> </div>That is a food for thought, but unless mundanes have access to it pretty much my point. I mean there are plenty of ways for Mages and a few other supernaturals to make a difference, but mundanes seem left with no recourse other than that big military grade weapon.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":". 02-13-2019, 06:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T16:16:09-08:00","id":1287732,"title":"","content":"Take the aiming penalty and apply arm wracks, leg wracks, what-have-yous. It's not always about amount of damage, Sometimes it's about how damage is applied","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9015-zee-patrick","name":"zee PaTrick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T16:20:59-08:00","id":1287735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zee PaTrick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1287660-mage-armor-piercing?p=1287732#post1287732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take the aiming penalty and apply arm wracks, leg wracks, what-have-yous. It's not always about amount of damage, Sometimes it's about how damage is applied</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem is you have to inflict enough damage to inflict the tilt. Which I believe is at least 2+ since it requires damage greater than the target's Stamina for wracks. So, not only at this point do you need to do at least 5+ damage in the event of Forces Armor. You also take a penalty on the small die pool you have. Not a good choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":".  Found the rules and edited my post, it is greater than for some hits. 02-13-2019, 07:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T16:22:17-08:00","id":1287738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1287660-mage-armor-piercing?p=1287681#post1287681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*shrugs* I mean, I guess if you have a military grade weapons you might be able to dent a mage. Forces 3 generates 3 armor which makes it pretty unlikely anything but a large military grade weapon will do anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two or more successes with a heavy handgun and you're through and dealing lethal damage. Hardly military grade stuff. It's tough to deal high amounts of damage, but that's just to be expected for magical means of protection.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My main concern is because Seers like to use proxies and it seems without having some pretty heavy packing proxies, there really is no point in having them at all. In 1E when armor could be dispelled it made proxy encounters orchestrated by Seers deadly, but now it is just like, &quot;Meh. I can throw up Forces Armor and your goons are going to need to pull out the military grade stuff just to scratch me.&quot; </div> </div> </div>It would be a real pain remotely dispell a mage's Mage Armor anyway. Even in first edition it should've been much easier to buff the proxy attackers instead. Subtly, in case they're Sleepers. I really don't see how it works in second edition would change how difficult it is for mundies to damage a prepared mage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because, again, even if you have AP bullets doesn't matter against mage armor. </div> </div> </div>Of the armor increasing Mage Armors I think only Matter Armor specifies that it ignores AP.<br /> <br /> You do have a point about the Defense increasing Mage Armors, as long as it stack with mundane Defense and Defense applies to the attack. The downside is that boosting Defense does absolutely nothing against direct damage dealing spells (unless you cast aimed spells).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1287660-mage-armor-piercing?p=1287703#post1287703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it helps, I'm pretty certain that direct damage spells bypass Mage Armor (except for Prime), so there's that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true for the Defense increasing Mage Armors (with the caveat for aimed spells) but armor increasing Mage Armors can help depending on what the direct damage spell actually does. For example, a Matter damage dealing spell that assaults the subject by striking them with surrounding materials (which is how both published Matter attack spells works) will have its damage reduced by any Mage Armor that grants armor against kinetic or physical attacks, like both Forces and Matter Armor. Both Spirit and Death Armor also applies on such attacks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1287660-mage-armor-piercing?p=1287705#post1287705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You hit a Mage before they can get their armor up, then you never have to worry about piercing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>A prepared mage will always be a pain to deal with. Turns out the mage you've been shooting on is actually just an illusion (Forces 2 or Mind 2), a puppet (Life 2 or Matter 2), in a zone that bullets can't enter/penetrate (Forces 2, Matter 2 or Space 3), or actually in Twilight with a Twilight visibility spell (Death 3 or Spirit 3) all along. Neither option requiring Mage Armor and most being available to mages before they even get access to Mage Armor for that particular Arcanum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T16:27:44-08:00","id":1287742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1287660-mage-armor-piercing?p=1287735#post1287735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Problem is you have to inflict enough damage to inflict the tilt. Which I believe is at least 2+ since it requires damage greater than the target's Stamina for wracks. So, not only at this point do you need to do at least 5+ damage in the event of Forces Armor. You also take a penalty on the small die pool you have. Not a good choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>All Death does is down grade so all your damage gets through<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9015-zee-patrick","name":"zee PaTrick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T16:33:18-08:00","id":1287744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Two or more successes with a heavy handgun and you're through and dealing lethal damage. Hardly military grade stuff. It's tough to deal high amounts of damage, but that's just to be expected for magical means of protection. </div> </div> </div>True, but again, I guess it depends on the die pool and luck. They &quot;might&quot; be able to do 1 Lethal. I had no joke, a guy attacking a Mage with Forces 3 armor and had 10 Die pool, never once did they get more than 2 successes. Granted they had a light pistol, but that was an extremely accurate dude. Basically never did any damage the entire time. So, I mean your mileage may vary, but it was very interesting and luck can be like that, but I don't expect every gun toting thug to have 5 Firearms and 5 Dex either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It would be a real pain remotely dispell a mage's Mage Armor anyway. Even in first edition it should've been much easier to buff the proxy attackers instead. Subtly, in case they're Sleepers. I really don't see how it works in second edition would change how difficult it is for mundies to damage a prepared mage. </div> </div> </div>I believe in 1E Sleepers could unravel Mage Armor from seeing their bullets not bringing the target down, even the Fate armor which made the person extremely lucky bordered upon the vulgar depending on the attacks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of the armor increasing Mage Armors I think only Matter Armor specifies that it ignores AP. </div> </div> </div>You know... I never really thought about this specific phrase. I mean, one could argue they just felt it was redundant to mention this because from my understanding Armor Piercing doesn't work on supernatural armor of any kind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A prepared mage will always be a pain to deal with. Turns out the mage you've been shooting on is actually just an illusion (Forces 2 or Mind 2), a puppet (Life 2 or Matter 2), in a zone that bullets can't enter/penetrate (Forces 2, Matter 2 or Space 3), or actually in Twilight with a Twilight visibility spell (Death 3 or Spirit 3) all along. Neither option requiring Mage Armor and most being available to mages before they even get access to Mage Armor for that particular Arcanum. </div> </div> </div>These are fine, because that is spell control. Not really a concern of mine. My concern is that attainments cost no spell control and pretty much make mundane proxies useless unless they are extremely lucky or having very heavy weaponry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":".  Missed a quote tag 02-13-2019, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T16:35:41-08:00","id":1287746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zee PaTrick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1287660-mage-armor-piercing?p=1287742#post1287742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All Death does is down grade so all your damage gets through</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point, that works for those types of armor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T17:00:20-08:00","id":1287758,"title":"","content":"They still cost Mana and are still only situationally relevant. It most certainly does not make mundane proxies useless. You just've got to be smarter than going full frontal assault on one of the most powerful beings in the setting.<br /> Order/bribe/mind control a waiter to poison the mage at a mundane restaurant. Now they can't use any flashy spells to help save themselves without causing Paradox and fucking up their standing in the Consilium.<br /> Or have a proxy plant a bomb somewhere. They either bypass or overwhelm all Mage Armors. It doesn't even have to be a bomb. Cast a fun spell combined with Hung Spell on a mundane item that is hidden close to the mage's sanctum and release it when there's a fitting opportunity or just let the duration of Hung Spell run out.<br /> If you're set on using your crazed domestic terrorists in a shoot out, direct them towards mundane friends and family members instead of the mage directly. Or towards any Sleepwalker assistants, if the mage has any.<br /> And if you're still dead set on using armed violence directly against the mage, just buff the proxies. Have Exceptional Luck cause the next firearms attack gain a ridiculous amount of extra dice, 8 Again, and/or Rote action. Relinquish unsafely and recast the spell two more times on each proxy soldier and suddenly they'll tear through even a Master's Mage Armor during at least three rounds (as already cast spells don't deteriorate until after they've had an effect that can trigger Quiescence, and only one spell will be &quot;spent&quot; per attack).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T17:11:29-08:00","id":1287761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It most certainly does not make mundane proxies useless. You just've got to be smarter than going full frontal assault on one of the most powerful beings in the setting.<br /> Order/bribe/mind control a waiter to poison the mage at a mundane restaurant. Now they can't use any flashy spells to help save themselves without causing Paradox and fucking up their standing in the Consilium. </div> </div> </div>Depends on the mage, this could risk Paradox very true. I also considered this option. The Seers probably would do something sinister along these levels assuming you don't have a Paranoid mage, but it has a chance of working. This of course doesn't really work in all situations but you are accurate in this being a possibility and one you can't really re-use a lot since granted the next time they go eat at a restaurant there is always going to be that check for poison.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or have a proxy plant a bomb somewhere. They either bypass or overwhelm all Mage Armors. It doesn't even have to be a bomb. Cast a fun spell combined with Hung Spell on a mundane item that is hidden close to the mage's sanctum and release it when there's a fitting opportunity or just let the duration of Hung Spell run out. </div> </div> </div>Bombs are messy, again this also refers to heavy weaponry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you're set on using your crazed domestic terrorists in a shoot out, direct them towards mundane friends and family members instead of the mage directly. Or towards any Sleepwalker assistants, if the mage has any. </div> </div> </div>This is a viable option in the event they can find out about their background. This might be for a dedicated Seer that has been working on a plan for sometime and is also another option, but again can be used sparingly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if you're still dead set on using armed violence directly against the mage, just buff the proxies. Have Exceptional Luck cause the next firearms attack gain a ridiculous amount of extra dice, 8 Again, and/or Rote action. Relinquish unsafely and recast the spell two more times on each proxy soldier and suddenly they'll tear through even a Master's Mage Armor during at least three rounds (as already cast spells don't deteriorate until after they've had an effect that can trigger Quiescence, and only one spell will be &quot;spent&quot; per attack). </div> </div> </div>This is what I have actually decided upon doing. It is possible to sneak this past since the thugs might just think these are good weapons from the &quot;right&quot; guy. It requires the least amount of effort and still makes mundane proxies a threat at all times against mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T17:45:13-08:00","id":1295422,"title":"","content":"This is simply bad form.<br /> <br /> A pack of, say, 3 werewolves or a group of 3 vampires would make short work of a &quot;group of thugs.&quot; Both werewolves and vampires have *innate* regeneration and defensive powers that not only make small-arms wielded by thugs laughably ineffective, but also outclass mages armors *with innate, baseline powers* until the mage hits gnosis 4 minimum. The only time a mage can truthfully be said to outclass werewolf/vampire innate passives it at Gnosis 5+. <br /> <br /> Trying to frame mages as unfairly hard to kill is narrowminded at least, if not deliberately untruthful. <br /> By the time Mages surpass Werewolves and Vampires defensively, they are Master Mages and are rivaled by Elder Vampires and Chieftain Werewolves: all of which treat normal human thugs like snacks. <br /> <br /> So complaining about mage armor while ignoring the fact that all other supers minimalize the threat of thugs... Well, see above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13668-horned-god","name":"Horned God","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T20:52:57-08:00","id":1295467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horned God</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1287660-mage-armor-piercing?p=1295422#post1295422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is simply bad form.<br /> <br /> A pack of, say, 3 werewolves or a group of 3 vampires would make short work of a &quot;group of thugs.&quot; Both werewolves and vampires have *innate* regeneration and defensive powers that not only make small-arms wielded by thugs laughably ineffective, but also outclass mages armors *with innate, baseline powers* until the mage hits gnosis 4 minimum. The only time a mage can truthfully be said to outclass werewolf/vampire innate passives it at Gnosis 5+.<br /> <br /> Trying to frame mages as unfairly hard to kill is narrowminded at least, if not deliberately untruthful.<br /> By the time Mages surpass Werewolves and Vampires defensively, they are Master Mages and are rivaled by Elder Vampires and Chieftain Werewolves: all of which treat normal human thugs like snacks.<br /> <br /> So complaining about mage armor while ignoring the fact that all other supers minimalize the threat of thugs... Well, see above.</div> </div> </div> </div>While it was not mentioned in the post originally this was assuming 1 Mage, not 2-3. However, the power scale is quite different when you look at the individual capabilities of 1 Mage, 1 Werewolf, 1 Vampire. So, lets do a power breakdown to analyze the weaknesses/strengths of each power splat.<br /> <br /> Werewolves have Gauru form which allows them to regenerate all lethal damage at the end of the round and is quite a useful regeneration. Now, Gauru is the war form and the ultimate form a Werewolf would transform into when fighting, so this seems feasible for this scenario. Now, in Gauru form they are allowed their Defense Against Firearms, so let's assume they have 3 Athletics and Wits &amp; Dex both at 3 so that gives them 6 Defense. They also get Down &amp; Dirty Combat with all mortals, meaning they can pretty much shred apart any mortal that decides to get in their way. Let's be fair and say half (5 out of 10) the humans manage to not lose it from the Lunacy and they open fire on the werewolf. Now, the werewolf is not wearing any armor and do not get any while in Gauru form so all they have is their defense. The humans have around 7-8 (spending a WP) dice to start with and let's say they use autofire for an additional +3 allowing them (11 Dice - 6 Defense) 5 dice against the werewolf. Let's say they all hit with at least 1 or 2 successes and werewolves don't get any resistance to bullets from my understanding, thus the werewolf is on average downed the first round of combat (10 Thugs = 12 Lethal at least with at least 5 of the scared thugs dealing a total of ~3-5 damage). Over. Maybe next time Werewolf.<br /> <br /> Let's go with the Vampire, see if maybe they fair better since they convert gunfire into bashing damage innately as the defense you mentioned in your post. Vampires don't really have any real forms, but they can &quot;ride the beast&quot; which allows them much more power in order to take on a bunch of humans. Unlike the Werewolves, they don't get lunacy so all 10 of these humans get to unload on the Vampire. Now, let's say the Vampire has some good Resilience, perhaps 2 (starting Vampire after all), so they have a total of 9 Health. The Vampire also for good measure has Celerity, allowing them to add 1 Point of Defense against firearms. The Vampire rolls unluckily and gets attacked by all the thugs using their autofire (11 Dice - 1 Defense) granting 10 dice so they on average score around 3-4 successes. Now, the Vampire does have Resilience and can spend 1 point of Vitae to subtract damage much as if they were wearing armor granting them 3/0 General Armor against the thugs. They take maybe 2 Bashing Damage and proceed to attack next round, perhaps using Obfuscate much like a Mage to slaughter their opponents by the time it is all said and done. So, Vampire wins taking minimal damage.<br /> <br /> Alright, now let's take a Mage to see if maybe they can fair a bit better against mortals. Now, the Mage has Space Armor, also has a Decent amount of Wits/Dex + Athletics giving them a total of 9 (starting Mage). Ok, so the Mage much like everyone else does not get to go the first round so all the thugs fire on him. Well, with a die pool of 2 (11 Dice - 9 Defense) you might get 1 success out of every 2-3 thugs. Let's be generous and say the thugs manage to score a total of 4 Lethal Damage against the Mage. The Mage can also reflexively spend mana to send the attack back at the target, potentially killing them and doing so takes out of a couple of thugs next turn. Sure, they may have taken 4 lethal damage, but there are now 2 less thugs and their turn begins. On the Mage's turn they decide to use Incognito Presence (Mastigos Mage with the Space Armor) and stealthily kills the remaining thugs. Mage wins, albeit taking the most damage. However, they would have been very similar to a Vampire had it been a general armor Mage allowing them to completely negate the damage suffered all together.<br /> <br /> I am not sure what you are talking about regarding power scale. If you have some more examples of 1 Werewolf/Vampire surviving against a group of thugs, by all means please present them. But there are several conditions that must be met in your examples: They must be starting supernatural being (no experience), they don't get initiative the first round (let's say the thugs get the drop on them), there are 10 thugs, and no one has armor currently equipped. I used 10 thugs because that was the amount I had originally intended to have in the encounter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":". 03-09-2019, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T00:55:58-07:00","id":1295747,"title":"","content":"I do not know how your games work, but a group of 10 npcs with automatic weapons and all spending willpower in the first round shooting at a Werewolf in gauru is no group of thugs in my game. That is a trained military kill squat. Also: defense lowers by one die with every consecutiv attack. So the Mage is very very dead at the end of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T03:51:10-07:00","id":1295750,"title":"","content":"I had forgotten about this rule since you typically normally apply your defense to melee or thrown attacks. Fair point, so the General Armor Mage is the only one capable of surviving this onslaught then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T06:17:36-07:00","id":1295782,"title":"","content":"That vampire can't hope to win the fight, only to get away before entering Torpor. Unlike Incognito Presence, Obfuscate can easily be seen through since everyone will look for the vampire and only get a -1 to their Wits+Composure. They also can't have 2 Resilience, 1 Celerity and 1 Obfuscate as a starting vampire.<br /> Also, a group of ten people will score ~36 successes (10*(1/3)+11*(1/3)*9) on average, adding 20 extra for the damage modifier for a whooping 56 damage. Subtract 30 from Resilience and you're down at 26 bashing. Even at max Stamina and with Giant that's full lethal. Down. Most starting vamps with that Discipline spread will be a single Health box from full aggravated.<br /> Wht the vampire should do is use Celerity to interrupt and get the hell out of Dodge. Taking damage from throwing yourself out of a window would be much better despite not being able to use Resilience the same turn.<br /> <br /> The mage is even more dead, though, as they take lethal rather than bashing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-11-2019, 09:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T08:13:35-07:00","id":1295826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1287660-mage-armor-piercing?p=1295782#post1295782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That vampire can't hope to win the fight, only to get away before entering Torpor. Unlike Incognito Presence, Obfuscate can easily be seen through since everyone will look for the vampire and only get a -1 to their Wits+Composure. They also can't have 2 Resilience, 1 Celerity and 1 Obfuscate as a starting vampire.<br /> Also, a group of ten people will score ~36 successes (10*(1/3)+11*(1/3)*9) on average, adding 20 extra for the damage modifier for a whooping 56 damage. Subtract 30 from Resilience and you're down at 26 bashing. Even at max Stamina and with Giant that's full lethal. Down. Most starting vamps with that Discipline spread will be a single Health box from full aggravated.<br /> Wht the vampire should do is use Celerity to interrupt and get the hell out of Dodge. Taking damage from throwing yourself out of a window would be much better despite not being able to use Resilience the same turn.<br /> <br /> The mage is even more dead, though, as they take lethal rather than bashing.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, I forgot my own rule they can't have the 2 Resilience, 1 Celerity, and 1 Obfuscate.<br /> <br /> Your rolls may vary, I used a simulator to roll 10 times with 10 dice and received on average a few 1 successes and a few 3 successes and 1 exceptional success.<br /> <br /> I did forget the automatic damage, and with an SMG, small (+1L) that totals about ~7-12 Bashing damage for the vampire, which would bleed over into 0-3 Lethal worse case scenario from my simulator of rolling.<br /> <br /> The Mage, you are correct would most likely suffer in the range between ~7-12 lethal damage making them either grievously injured or most likely dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T08:15:19-07:00","id":1295828,"title":"","content":"Tessie has done the statistics which is going to be superior to an anecdotal test.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T09:13:34-07:00","id":1295846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1287660-mage-armor-piercing?p=1295828#post1295828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tessie has done the statistics which is going to be superior to an anecdotal test.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true, but I don\u2019t use averages when I play I use the results as rolled. So I like to consider luck a large part of it. Either way the Vampire is still alive given the parameters, so I am not sure what your point is. Because 46 damage reduced by 30 is 16 bashing, a survivable attack for a 9-11 Health Vampire. We already corrected a Mage would die.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T10:23:29-07:00","id":1295866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1287660-mage-armor-piercing?p=1295846#post1295846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very true, but I don\u2019t use averages when I play I use the results as rolled.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you use the simulated rolls you already rolled, this makes absolutely no sense.<br /> <br /> Edit: You can't use simulated rolls to account for variance. You'll just end up creating more variance between your simulated rolls and the real rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-11-2019, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T10:45:05-07:00","id":1295869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1287660-mage-armor-piercing?p=1295866#post1295866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless you use the simulated rolls you already rolled, this makes absolutely no sense.<br /> <br /> Edit: You can't use simulated rolls to account for variance. You'll just end up creating more variance between your simulated rolls and the real rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright the actual results at the time of play was 26 successes.<br /> Thug 1: Scored 2 successes<br /> Thug 2: Scored 0 successes (funny I know)<br /> Thug 3: Scored 1 successes<br /> Thug 4: Scored 3 successes<br /> Thug 5: Scored 5 successes<br /> Thug 6: Scored 4 successes<br /> Thug 7: Scored 3 successes<br /> Thug 8: Scored 2 successes<br /> Thug 9: Scored 3 successes<br /> Thug 10: Scored 3 successes<br /> <br /> At the time I forgot to add the automatic damage resulting in a net total of 3 Lethal Damage was dealt. I now realize my folly and this should have actually been 9 Lethal damage which would have definitely changed things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":".  Added breakdown of thug successes and the results. I also corrected my math, I can't add apparently. Was all done on my phone at the time. 03-11-2019, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T11:12:39-07:00","id":1296182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1287660-mage-armor-piercing?p=1295846#post1295846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very true, but I don\u2019t use averages when I play I use the results as rolled. So I like to consider luck a large part of it. Either way the Vampire is still alive given the parameters, so I am not sure what your point is. Because 46 damage reduced by 30 is 16 bashing, a survivable attack for a 9-11 Health Vampire. We already corrected a Mage would die.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Luck&quot; is accounted for by statistics because probability. You don't even make any sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T11:41:30-07:00","id":1296189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1287660-mage-armor-piercing?p=1296182#post1296182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &amp;quot;Luck&amp;quot; is accounted for by statistics because probability. You don't even make any sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>To some degree it is accounted for, but obviously there are variances such as the 26 successes I rolled. Averages are a good baseline but that is about it because when it comes down to it the only real result that matters is a sample of 1. It helps give you an approximation but does not really tell you how the game will play out or how the dice will roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T11:55:57-07:00","id":1296192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1287660-mage-armor-piercing?p=1296189#post1296189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It helps give you an approximation but does not really tell you how the game will play out or how the dice will roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither does simulated rolls. You're only adding additional variance between your approximation and the end result by simulating rolls instead of using statistics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T12:14:17-07:00","id":1296195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1287660-mage-armor-piercing?p=1296192#post1296192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Neither does simulated rolls. You're only adding additional variance between your approximation and the end result by simulating rolls instead of using statistics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never really argued that you were incorrect on this statement. I simple used a simple simulator to determine the results on the fly and applied them to this situation. I never argued it was more accurate. I really don\u2019t understand why this is brought up. All I meant to argue was that averages are nice, but I tend to say let\u2019s see what happens. I never said averages were bad or that my simulated roll was the in stone fact of how that would end. It was a simple example of 1 scenario.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T13:01:55-07:00","id":1296210,"title":"","content":"The way you phrased it made it seem you purposefully wanted simulated rolls instead of the statistical average, not that you were fine with either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T13:05:46-07:00","id":1296211,"title":"","content":"Total misunderstanding then, I am very sorry you took it that way. It was not my intent to dismiss your averages, though I can see how that was derived. I just merely wanted to apply what you had pointed out accurately to my running scenario that I was basing things on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":". 03-12-2019, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T19:27:59-07:00","id":1296562,"title":"","content":"I think we can coclude that a 10 man gang armed with firearms that ambushes any starting supernatural is a deadly situation for the supernatural with minimal to moderate casualties for the gang. <br /> <br /> Personally, If I want to &quot;play out&quot; likely outcomes of a fight I create 3 scenarios a) Perfect Team A, b) Perfect Team B and c) Average<br /> <br /> In your example, a Perfect synchronized ambush that the mage failed to notice (and thus failed to cast or activate mage armor or apply defence) will end with him dead. A perfect mage scenario would be if he survives the first round (via NPC failed rolls or his own reactions) then find the right combo of spells to escape (forces 2, mind 2, ally spirit, artifact, etc) and/or retaliate, possible to eliminate all his enemies. <br /> <br /> These are edge cases though. Most of the time the situation will turn up somewhere in between and that's where &quot;average&quot; becomes important. It is an interesting thought and statistical experiment but I have to ask &quot;what kind of storyteller will ambush his starting players with 10 armed guys?&quot; <br /> <br /> Truth be told, I fell in the same trap too; doing numerical calculations of &quot;how many bad guys can my party fight at once&quot; when the question itself is wrong. In my case the correct question was &quot;what is this scene about?&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","name":"Shadowjim12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T19:40:10-07:00","id":1296565,"title":"","content":"Is this scene about your PCs discovering their newfound powers? Let them smash 5 police officers without a scratch. <br /> <br /> Is this scene about teaching them their limits? Have 20+ grapple them and beat them bashingly unconsious with disbelief and paradox creating chaos and them waking robed at the street or the hospital<br /> <br /> My point is the &quot;flavour&quot; of the scene is much more important than theorycrafting the mechanics since a storyteller can direct it either way, regardless of npc templates and numbers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","name":"Shadowjim12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T04:37:46-07:00","id":1296647,"title":"","content":"You make some good points, mostly this was apparently my lack of understanding all the mechanics involved in combat &amp; damage. Sure, I could overwhelm them with brute force or do this and that, but I felt I was missing something or something wasn't logically adding up in my head. I thought, perhaps Mage Armor was unbeatable, but as I found out from this thread there were many factors I had not been including. The scene in question was suppose to be a drug deal made between a Seer and a Pentacle member who was a really good &quot;cook&quot; and the Seer wanted his stuff. Seers, however, love using Proxies so I was trying to build that frame up from that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T12:03:50-07:00","id":1298375,"title":"","content":"For anyone curious here is the breakdown for survivability at least in Round 1 for the following scenario for a starting member of a splat based on 5 million simulations:<br /> Enemy Count: 10, Enemy Die Pool: 10, Enemy Weapon: Small SMG, No Die Tricks<br /> PC Health: 8, PC Base Defense: 3<br /> Mage with Force/Matter Armor: 7%<br /> Mage with Life Armor: 2%<br /> \u200bMage with Death/Spirit Armor: 0%<br /> Mage with Mind/Space/Fate/Time Armor: 0%<br /> Vampire with Resilience 2, Celerity 1: 42%<br /> Werewolf in Gauru Form: 1%<br /> <br /> Best be a Resilient Vampire. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T11:30:14-07:00","id":1298680,"title":"","content":"I generally feel that in baseline CofD guns aren't really as dangerous as one would asume they should be. Hurt Locker changed things by introducing the Bleeding tilt that really makes weapons way more dangerous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T12:04:08-07:00","id":1298695,"title":"","content":"I haven't added those effects into my simulations, but I am using an extremely high number of enemies. Perhaps with those added the threshold would be much much lower. Good point though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}